each year at commencement our university  recognizes an exceptional  individuals with honorary degrees these  degrees are the most significant  distinction conferred by the Yale  corporation the University's Board of  Trustees to signal pioneering  achievement in a field or conspicuous  and exemplary contribution to the common  good though we cannot adorn this year's  honorary degree recipients in their  academic hoods or applaud their  accomplishments as they stand on the  commencement stage we gather from our  computers phones and devices around the  world to recognize the ways in which  they have expanded our knowledge and  gifted us with their art song  scholarship and innovation today we  honor nine individuals who serve as  examples to our graduates and members of  the Yale community they encourage us to  aspire to excellence and to value those  elements of human character that they  embody creativity curiosity disciplined  integrity and a passion for public  service their association with the class  of 2020 also honors the students who  graduate today collectively they  represent the aspirations of Yale as an  institution it is now my distinct  pleasure to announce the 2020 honorary  degree recipients and to confer their  degrees for the degree of Doctor of Laws  to Rome Alan Cohen legal scholar  pioneering scholar of Chinese law you  have taught and mentored countless  others in a field you helped establish  in this country a courageous voice for  those whose voices have been silenced  you defend human rights around the globe  bold trailblazer and advocate for using  your many talents to create a more just  world we are  proud to present you with your third  Yale degree Doctor of Laws for the  degree of Doctor of music Herbie Hancock  musician and composer chameleon of  modern jazz you have shown us new  possibilities and encouraged us to  imagine a better world by experimenting  with science and sound  you let your talent take you and us to  new places breaking down barriers  between genres and creating chords of  peace that connect humanity Wonderful  Wizard and musical icon  Yale is delighted to confer on you this  Doctor of Music degree  for the degree of Doctor of Humane  Letters Christiana Figueres public  servant your diplomacy has brought  people and nations together to address  one of the most important issues of our  time climate change building bridges  instead of borders  you've led countries to action helping  forge international Accords to ensure  the health and survival future  generations on this planet global  citizen skilled leader yell is honored  to award you this Doctor of Humane  Letters degree for the degree of Doctor  of Engineering and Technology  Michael I Jordan computer scientist  facing an uncertain and complex world  you harness the power of human and  machine learning to solve daunting  problems by bridging disciplines and  following your curiosity you have made  possible what was once only imagined  Explorer of new domains champion of big  ideas and recognition of the doors who  have opened and the networks who have  built we proudly bestow on you this  doctor of Engineering and Technology  degree for the degree of Doctor of Fine  Arts Ming Jolie theatrical set designer  you have set the world on stage and your  influence circles the globe your  classroom is legendary with insight and  humility  you inspired thousands of Yale students  to create new vistas of art and meaning  generous teacher visionary artists for  helping a see feel and understand the  great drama of human life anew we're  delighted to confer on you this Doctor  of Fine Arts degree for the degree of  Doctor of  science savant a pabo evolutionary  geneticist from bone fragments thousands  of years old you show us what has  endured and what has been lost from  ancient times to the present day  applying the latest science to age-old  questions you have revealed secrets  about the prehistoric world discovered  previously unknown species and invented  a new field of study passionate  scientist for opening a window onto our  ancestors and ourselves Yale is  privileged to confer on you this Doctor  of Science degree for the degree of  doctor of music Renee Fleming soprano  you have shared your extraordinary voice  on the world's greatest stages thrilling  audiences with your repertoire and range  transcending styles and traditions you  champion the importance of music for our  health  minds and communities soaring soprano  lyrical ambassador of the Arts for  helping us here all the octaves of life  more clearly we are honored to present  you with this Doctor of Music degree for  the degree of doctor of Medical Sciences  Jim Allison immunologist your  discoveries have transformed the science  of cancer treatment opening up new  frontiers in medicine by unleashing the  power of t-cells you enlisted the body's  own immune system to combat this  terrible disease and your research has  restored health and hope to patients  laureate and lifeline in honor of the  futures you have made possible with  gratefully bestow on you  this doctor of Medical Sciences degree  and for the degree of Doctor of Letters  Paula Vogel playwright and educator  while waltzing or driving dying or  loving your characters connect with  audiences and bring urgent issues out of  the shadows a devoted teacher you foster  the future of theater helping young  playwrights find their voices and refine  their craft an appreciation for your  brave artistry and spirited mentorship  Yale is proud to award you this Doctor  of Letters degree  I send my warm congratulations to all of  you the entire university joins me in  applauding your accomplishments welcome  to the class of 2020
 

